{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D81-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"0647a2b1ae01f774449ead7ed5289b641cb06163c4fb01e33e3c79d58906c20e\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 demands recognition that the year mattered; A5 separates packing the photo from dismissing the memory.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's reduction to a picture; A5 accepts B4's acknowledgment, although A3's 'paper' is oblique.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants to treat packing practically; B4 supplies the emotional recognition A needs to cooperate.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"After B4 names their happiness, A5 permits packing while explicitly protecting its significance.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes shared packing around a particular photo; B4 locates happiness there without identifying the occasion.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 earns its 'packing that away' turn from A1's box and B4's acknowledgment.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before you box that photo, tell me that year mattered.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's only a picture.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then say what isn't in the paper.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We were happy there.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Good. Now we can pack the picture without packing that away.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D81 makes A secure acknowledgment of shared significance before allowing an object associated with that history to be treated practically.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D83 tests accurate recall; D81 requires recognition that what happened mattered.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 asks whether the year mattered, and B4's emotional acknowledgment satisfies A5 without any factual memory examination.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a accepts packing once meaning is recognized; alternative b challenges disposal and recruits shared sacrifice as grounds for preserving a token.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after a separate internal reread: the original still earns 86 with the same dimension ratings and cited evidence. B4 changes A5 from withholding cooperation to granting it with an emotional distinction. All five-turn and causal gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A3's reference to 'paper' is slightly literary, and the shared year remains unspecified; the emotional negotiation is nevertheless playable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D81-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"5692c65f19538ca8bf08f681729f03ab30d84b352142c414d59dbe395ecf87a6\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 names months of saving; A5 insists the ticket represents more than cardboard.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 tests B2's claim to remember, but A5 gives B4's missed-boat story only a generic 'Exactly'.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 answer A's prompts; neither gives B a clear reason to discard the ticket.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 restates A1's significance claim without developing what staying after the missed boat meant.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies saving for a trip and A3 a ticket being discarded; B4 offers a playable shared mishap.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 and A5 efficiently contrast sacrifice with a disposable object, though A5 is predictable.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 76\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before you bin our ferry ticket, remember the Saturdays we worked to afford that trip.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We missed the ferry. It's proof we wasted money.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You said staying on the dock with me was worth every Saturday.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It was. But this scrapbook is full.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then take out my graduation certificate. That only took me three years.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D81 makes A defend a shared experience's importance by requiring B to weigh it against apparently more substantial achievements.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Sentimental hoarding protects objects indiscriminately; D81 seeks another person's acknowledgment of the relationship or sacrifice they represent.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 invokes B's valuation of their time together, and A5 sacrifices A's own certificate after B4 acknowledges that value.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a permits storage after verbal acknowledgment; revised b accepts limited space but argues for shared history through a personal sacrifice.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised because original A5 barely uses B4 and B lacks a disposal motive. The new illustrative setting adds a full scrapbook. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 demands recognition of shared sacrifice), logic 5 (A3 answers B2's wasted money; A5 uses B4's capacity limit), relationship 4 (B4 recognizes value while retaining a practical need), heightening 4 (A5 offers a personally costly substitution), specificity 5 (A1's ferry ticket and A5's certificate are playable), brevity/wit 4 (A5's comparison grows from A1's Saturdays). Total 92; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 deliberately overvalues the weekend against graduation; it needs sincere delivery to remain a bid for recognition rather than a glib comparison.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D82-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"42dc4b76a93de2bf29a37f86a6a8b09fae047ec9a2e43f9d93b5209c730ba3d8\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 explicitly asks B to choose their conversation over work; A3 treats the competing importance as the point.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's 'important' to increase the value of choosing them; A5 directly specifies B4's offered ten minutes.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 defends work and B4 negotiates a bounded postponement, materially changing A's request.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 converts B4's scheduling concession into a request for undivided attention.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes an interrupted conversation with a ringing work call; the conversation's subject remains open.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's reversal of 'important' is concise and motivated; A5 earns its phone detail from A1.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Leave the work call ringing. Stay with this conversation.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's important.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then choosing us would mean something.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll call back in ten minutes.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Good. Give these ten minutes to me without watching the phone.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D82 makes A turn a competing obligation into a concrete opportunity for B to prioritize their connection.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Demanding attention alone need not involve a rival commitment; D82 specifically requires choosing the relationship over one.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 uses the work call's importance as the reason choosing 'us' matters, and A5 claims the interval B4 makes available.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a bargains over a short interruption and develops B's compromise; alternative b asks B to surrender an evening's professional opportunity.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after an internal reread at 90 with unchanged ratings and evidence. B4's helpful concession creates A5's more exact request for presence, so agreement continues the card rather than ending it. Hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The nature of the relationship and interrupted conversation are unspecified, and the scene's strength is its negotiation rather than a large comic payoff.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D82-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"007465bc301196f80451ed47ce387b7e1137c7366cf2591242213053c7f56abe\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 asks B to skip networking for their evening; A5 explicitly asks whether the relationship comes first.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 counters B2's unrepeatable opportunity; A5 uses B4's tomorrow proposal, albeit abstractly.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 presents a credible opportunity cost and B4 offers an alternative date.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 broadens the complaint to 'ever' without adding a concrete choice beyond A1.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 names a networking dinner, but A3's 'tonight exactly like this' supplies no particular shared circumstance.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 and A5 sound like polished relationship maxims rather than discoveries within this evening.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 79\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Stay for our anniversary dinner. Your networking badge is sitting in the gravy.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The investor leaves tomorrow. I could get the bakery funded tonight.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I helped you knead at four this morning. Tonight I'd like to be your husband.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Come with me. I'll introduce you as my cofounder.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Introduce me as the reason you're leaving before dessert.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D82 makes A press B to give their marriage priority when a professional opportunity threatens to absorb their shared occasion.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D81 asks for recognition of past contribution; D82 uses any such contribution to obtain a present choice in favor of the connection.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Although A3 mentions helping at dawn, A5's goal is B leaving the investor event for their relationship, not praising that help.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a secures protected minutes at home; revised b negotiates public acknowledgment and an early departure after B offers inclusion in the competing event.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the original's abstract stakes into an illustrative married bakery partnership on an anniversary. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A5 seeks an actual priority choice), logic 5 (A3 responds to B2's bakery goal; A5 transforms B4's introduction), relationship 4 (B offers inclusion while pursuing funding), heightening 4 (A5 accepts attendance conditionally and asks for visible commitment), specificity 5 (A1 establishes dinner and the badge), brevity/wit 4 (A5 repurposes the introduction). Total 92; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The anniversary increases A's apparent moral advantage, and the badge in gravy needs to remain incidental domestic detail rather than demand stage business.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D83-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"f3c1705f1867cdb87811b04353fdd145785b8165845568e80bc77bf1672c05c5\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 quizzes cup preference, A3 supplies a clue, and A5 introduces a second preference test.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 corrects B2's indifference; A5 advances after B4's blue-cup answer, though milk could follow any correct answer.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 function mainly as quiz responses without a separate practical aim.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds another ordinary question but little changed pressure after B4.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes tea preparation and A3 gives the cup twelve years of history.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Let's see how the memory travels' explains the testing behavior already visible in A1.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 77\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You're making my tea? Which mug is mine?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The blue one. I've already put two sugars in.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Two? What did I give up when we got married?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Sugar. I'll make another. Just tell me how you want it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll give you a clue: what have you complained about me doing to the teabag for twelve years?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D83 makes A turn an ordinary favor into successive small tests of whether B remembers A's preferences and their shared history.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Correcting an incorrectly made drink would supply the answer; D83 keeps requiring B to retrieve it.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 asks B to remember giving up sugar, and A5 answers B4's request for instructions with another memory clue.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a tests domestic preferences during a helpful task; alternative b tests authorship and wording of a story they have told together.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised because original B had little agency and A5 explained the game. The illustrative tea setting now specifies a marriage. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 make small tests), logic 5 (B2's sugar error prompts A3; B4's request prompts A5's clue), relationship 4 (B wants to remake the tea efficiently), heightening 4 (A5 tests a remembered complaint instead of accepting direct repair), specificity 5 (mug, sugar and teabag are concrete), brevity/wit 4 (A5 recruits B's own complaint as evidence). Total 92; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A's refusal to give a simple brewing instruction can feel punitive unless played as a sincere wish to be known.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D83-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"5c0875e1c45e19072f68eb61fbaa45057848e804c54e58f81bc529214d40c05c5\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 and A3 test shared history, but A5 abandons testing for a statement of disappointment.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 follows B2's missed boat to the dock; A5 responds directly to B4's failure to remember.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 supply answers but no reason for recalling the story or resisting the test.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"After B4 fails, A5 comments on diminished recall without creating a further test or choice.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 names a first holiday and boat, but there is no present occasion for telling the story.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 is concise and emotionally intelligible, but supplies a familiar wistful observation rather than developing A3's test.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 67\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before you tell our ferry story at dinner, what did I say when we missed it?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You said we could swim. I always get a laugh with that.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That was you. What did I say about your suitcase?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I forget. Could you tell that bit tonight?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll start it. But you're finishing the sentence about what you packed instead of clothes.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D83 makes A check whether B can accurately reconstruct their shared story instead of merely repeat its familiar comic outline.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D81 seeks acknowledgment that a memory mattered; D83 demands accurate details through small tests.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 corrects who suggested swimming and tests the suitcase detail; A5 turns B4's proposed handoff into another completion test.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Revised b gives the tests a public storytelling purpose and allows B to seek help; revised a tests private domestic knowledge during tea preparation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised because original A5 stopped testing. Added the illustrative occasion of telling their story at dinner. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 test exact details), logic 5 (A3 corrects B2; A5 modifies B4's handoff), relationship 4 (B wants a successful story and asks A to contribute), heightening 4 (A5 makes B complete the shared account at dinner), specificity 4 (ferry and suitcase are clear, contents remain open), brevity/wit 4 (A5 promises a concrete revealing detail without an unrelated joke). Total 90; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The suitcase contents remain unspecified, so the scene earns its turn through the test and changed responsibility rather than a completed anecdote.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D84-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d955b2fe1f6fba0d3f9e54b0dbb0652bd59f0d03cd98684730eaf1f2393987e6\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 and A3 ask B to relinquish an ongoing emotional charge while allowing the argument to be remembered.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 distinguishes forgetting from B2's objection; A5 answers B4's concern about the argument recurring.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants the hurt remembered, but neither B2 nor B4 identifies the actual unresolved grievance.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 restates the boundary using a chair metaphor rather than changing what B could do at dinner.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1's 'demand for payment' does not identify playable behavior; A5's displaced chair remains figurative.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1, A3 and A5 accumulate payment, interest, visiting and seating metaphors around an unspecified argument.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 66\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Will you sit beside me at dinner? You've left that chair empty since I forgot our anniversary.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Sitting there would look like I've forgiven you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You can still be angry beside me. I miss passing you things.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll sit there, but I'm not making conversation.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Would you pass me the potatoes? We can start with things that don't need forgiving.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D84 makes A persuade B to surrender a concrete form of resentment-maintained distance so their relationship can move again.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Seeking blanket absolution asks B to erase the grievance; D84 can instead seek release of one obstructive claim or distancing behavior.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 explicitly permits anger while asking for proximity, and A5 uses B4's seating concession to invite a small exchange.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Revised a seeks physical proximity and ordinary cooperation; alternative b seeks permission to be useful despite a remembered failure.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Replaced abstract dinner metaphors with an illustrative anniversary grievance and empty adjacent chair. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1 targets sustained distance), logic 5 (A3 answers B2's forgiveness concern; A5 respects B4's conversational limit), relationship 4 (B negotiates proximity without absolution), heightening 4 (A5 moves from seating to reciprocal contact), specificity 5 (A1's empty chair makes the impasse visible), brevity/wit 4 (A5 earns the potato request from A3's wish to pass things). Total 92; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"Passing potatoes is deliberately modest progress; its consequence depends on actors giving the established distance emotional weight.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D84-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"64bfbbe3c7c29d5a7260e4e28f30f0d2a401b5c309b104636e9a2ef90e778876\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 allows B to name the hurt while asking B to stop using it to block present help.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's continuing hurt; A5 narrows B4's accusation of wanting a clean slate.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 protects an unresolved injury and B4 challenges the terms of A's proposed repair.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 reframes the same request with 'today's date' but does not specify any newly available action.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a missed birthday, but A3 never identifies the help currently being refused.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's slate response grows directly from B4, though its polish exceeds its practical specificity.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 81\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Let me carry a box. Missing your birthday shouldn't mean I can't help you move.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I needed you then. Now I've hired movers.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'm not asking you to cancel them. Give me something they aren't carrying.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The cake tin. It still has your slice in it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then let me wash it at your new place. Don't make that slice the last thing you ever save me.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D84 makes A negotiate release from a past failure's continuing power to exclude A from the relationship.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Offering restitution alone concerns repayment; D84 asks B to stop maintaining a grievance as a barrier to renewed connection.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 challenges exclusion from helping, and A5 uses the preserved slice to ask for a future beyond the missed birthday.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Revised b pursues access through practical service during a move; revised a accepts lingering anger while seeking ordinary closeness at dinner.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised to specify the help and make B4 supply a consequential object. The new illustrative setting is B's move. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A5 asks B to release permanent exclusion), logic 5 (A3 accommodates B2's movers; A5 addresses B4's cake tin), relationship 4 (B has arranged alternatives and retains a pointed grievance), heightening 4 (A5 asks for a role in the new home), specificity 5 (boxes, movers and tin support play), brevity/wit 3 (A5's saved-slice image is emotionally clear but polished). Total 90; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The retained slice implies a relatively recent birthday, and A5's wording still risks sounding composed rather than discovered.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D85-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"b77563ba84a5832a5551d9ca5e4e225f2e170fc53c0d3474d2eef877a824a9f2\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 and A5 evade A's role identified in B2, but A1's stationery offer conveys little urgency.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 redirects B2 toward restarting; A5 refuses the explanation B4 requests using the established page.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 identifies A's responsibility and B4 seeks an explanation before resuming contact.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats the restart-over-explanation tactic without increasing A's repair effort.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's fresh stationery gives the reunion a concrete medium; B2 establishes unanswered letters.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's refusal to spend the first page on the gap grows from A1's offered stationery.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 77\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've brought stamps. Write to me before you move tomorrow; I want us back.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You never answered my last six letters.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The post has been hopeless. I'll collect this one myself.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I put those six through your door.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then hand this one straight to me. I'll answer while you're still holding the other end.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D85 makes A urgently rebuild contact while concealing responsibility for having broken it.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D86 merely redirects discussion away from why the relationship changed; D85 additionally conceals A's agency while actively pursuing repair.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"B2 identifies A's unanswered letters, A3 blames delivery, and A5 escalates immediate correspondence when B4 dismantles that excuse.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Revised a uses a failing postal excuse and an imminent move; alternative b uses domestic hospitality and access to conceal deliberate exclusion.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised to make urgency and concealment explicit. Added an illustrative move tomorrow while preserving correspondence. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 conceals responsibility while A1 and A5 urgently seek contact), logic 5 (A3 answers B2's six letters; A5 adapts to B4's hand delivery), relationship 4 (B corrects the excuse with direct knowledge), heightening 5 (A5 promises a reply before physical handover finishes), specificity 4 (stamps, door and move are clear), brevity/wit 4 (A5 literalizes an immediate reply). Total 93; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A3's delivery excuse is transparently weak; sincerity must reside in A's need to reconnect, not in an expectation that B will believe it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D85-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"c24fa4901b6c00ecc908f35c736f509fda8531b22beb4fa4877776dad47f6f15\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 offers restored access and A3 evades changing the lock, but A5's tea does not establish urgent repair.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 redirects B2 to the working key; A5 responds to B4's months outside with intensified welcome.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 asks why access changed and B4 reveals prolonged exclusion rather than simply accepting hospitality.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'especially welcoming' tea is a small verbal increase after B4's substantial grievance.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a new key and returning visitor; B4 gives the exclusion a duration.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's focus on the working key neatly evades B2; A5's tea is concise but familiar.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 77\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Here's your new key, Mum. Please stay; your tea's already poured.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Why did you change the lock without telling me?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Security got complicated. I've put your biscuit tin back by the kettle.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You told the locksmith not to give me a copy.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll have him bring you three. Please take your coat off while I ring.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D85 makes A conceal deliberate distancing by urgently supplying increasingly generous signs of restored access.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"An open apology would acknowledge A's role; D85 repairs while preserving evasion of that role.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 substitutes vague security trouble for personal agency, and A5 responds to B4's proof with more keys rather than an admission.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Revised b uses a parent-child visit, hospitality and overcompensation; revised a uses correspondence, a delivery excuse and a departure deadline.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the mild tea escalation into an urgent access offer. Added an illustrative mother-child relationship and locksmith evidence. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 hides agency and A5 pleads for continued presence), logic 5 (A3 evades B2; A5 recruits the locksmith B4 identifies), relationship 4 (B knows A's specific exclusionary instruction), heightening 4 (A5 multiplies keys and offers immediate action), specificity 5 (key, coat and biscuit tin establish the visit), brevity/wit 4 (three keys overcompensate for withheld access). Total 92; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The history could suggest reasonable boundaries as well as wrongdoing; the scene leaves that history open and plays A's current concealment without adjudicating it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D86-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"71ab3d48045c14fdfcded36d74a34d784c5d69dc0d3104d38ee0b7b5f9e47b8d\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 substitutes condiments for B2's stopped communication; A5 again avoids B4's direct question about disappearing.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 can follow almost any uncomfortable B2, and A5's 'both' principally answers A3's own condiment options.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 names the rupture and B4 insists on its cause, providing a credible competing conversational aim.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 moves from remembering sandwiches to proposing their recovery as a substitute for explanation.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a shared picnic memory and A3 gives concrete food details.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's recovery of sandwiches follows the food diversion, although B4 contributes little to its exact form.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 82\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've brought sandwiches for our first picnic in a year. Same filling?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Last time, I told you I was moving in with Ruth. You left.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Does Ruth like pickle? I can make her one.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"She's coming. We both want to know why you stopped calling.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then I'd better label the sandwiches. Three people reaching for the wrong thing gets awkward.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D86 makes A redirect each approach to the relationship's real rupture into safe practical conversation.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D85 requires hiding A's responsibility while urgently repairing distance; D86 can accept the factual history while blocking discussion of its reason.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 uses Ruth's name without disputing A's departure, and A5 uses her arrival to divert B4's request for an explanation into sandwich logistics.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Revised a diverts through hospitality when a third person becomes imminent; alternative b converts the timing of a past argument into a film-resumption plan.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised because original A3 and A5 drew too little from their preceding B turns. Added an illustrative reunion picnic and Ruth's impending arrival. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 avoid the cause), logic 5 (A3 uses B2's Ruth; A5 uses B4's third attendee), relationship 4 (B presses for an explanation shared by Ruth), heightening 4 (A5 expands the diversion to managing three people), specificity 5 (picnic, filling and arrival are playable), brevity/wit 3 (A5's awkwardness wording slightly advertises the subtext). Total 90; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A's final phrase carries a conspicuous double meaning; it should sound like a sincere practical concern rather than commentary on the scene.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D86-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"8aeb6c4acb4b6f3c82d6dd02d2a885a6ca0e403a8a43c9a2fc741c09626f0ce2\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 avoids B2's question about stopped meetings; A5 redirects B4's argument into the film's starting position.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 offers the unfinished shared comedy in response to B2; A5 specifically appropriates B4's 'halfway'.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 seeks discussion and B4 names A's walkout, challenging the comfortable activity A proposes.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 converts B4's more explicit accusation into a concrete plan that continues avoiding it.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes choosing a film together; A3 gives an unfinished comedy and B4 its uncomfortable association.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's halfway restart depends on B4's phrasing, though 'Efficient reunion' is slightly self-conscious.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Let's choose a film like we used to.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Can we discuss why we stopped meeting?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"We never finished that comedy.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You walked out halfway through our argument.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then we'll start the film at halfway. Efficient reunion.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D86 makes A repurpose B's attempts to discuss the rupture into harmless decisions about a shared activity.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D89 positively reframes a rupture as beneficial; D86 sidesteps evaluating the rupture at all.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A5 does not claim walking out helped them; it transfers B4's halfway point to the film so the argument can remain undiscussed.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b uses a temporal detail to redirect into entertainment; revised a absorbs an impending third person's arrival into hospitality logistics.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after an internal reread at 90 with the original dimension ratings and evidence unchanged. B4 gives A5 the exact restarting tactic; the closing proposal remains available for B to resist. Hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The last two words are more epigrammatic than natural, and the shared film's relationship to the argument is left implicit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D87-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"82d545a3e768790d2f1ef13456cf540140e220a83562db1fc7a09c1861ae90f8\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A3 hides an unpleasant detail, but A1 and A5 establish protecting breakfast rather than fear the relationship cannot survive conflict.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 acknowledges B2's letter; A5 repeats B4's 'changed' without using the brother's actual plans.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 notices concealment and B4 guesses a recurring issue, but the consequences between A and B remain unstated.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats the egg diversion from A3 without a stronger protective tactic or new relational risk.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 supplies a letter under a plate, but B4's changed plans are never identified.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's reliable eggs connect verbally to B4 but make the secret feel like a breakfast inconvenience.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 52\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"My brother's letter can wait. We've only just started having breakfast together again.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Has he asked to move back in? Last time I nearly left you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"He's asking about the spare room. It doesn't have to become another row.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Then I'll ring and tell him it's still my office.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Please don't. Let me answer him. I can't face your suitcase by the door again.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D87 makes A conceal the full truth of a recurring conflict because A believes another confrontation could end the relationship.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary conflict avoidance seeks comfort; D87 specifically protects a relationship A believes is near breaking.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"B2 identifies a previous near-departure, A3 reduces the request to spare-room questions, and A5 links blocking direct verification to the feared suitcase.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Revised a uses a concealed family housing request and a threatened phone call; alternative b conceals A's own action through selective financial disclosure.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised because the original omitted the card's essential survival motive. The illustrative breakfast now concerns a brother's return and a previous near-separation. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 minimizes the truth and A5 names fear of departure), logic 5 (A3 evades B2's specific question; A5 blocks B4's verification), relationship 4 (B protects office space and proposes direct resolution), heightening 4 (A5 must prevent contact rather than merely delay reading), specificity 5 (letter, spare room and suitcase ground the stakes), brevity/wit 3 (clear tension takes precedence over a comic payoff). Total 90; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The full housing request is strongly implied rather than admitted, and A's final plea is emotionally direct enough to make the scene more tense than comic.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D87-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"851b2ddcbf337ec6eb7f3f46282414d18e125fd1bb0e039fa4262c7cc2dbf1db\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 and A5 conceal information for a quiet evening and tea; neither establishes fear of losing the relationship.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's long-version question evasively; A5 narrows B4's objection to hiding everything.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 objects to concealment, but B2 has no concrete truth to pursue or practical stake to defend.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 reduces the objective to finishing tea rather than increasing the consequences of A3's concealment.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1's short version and A3's several reasons never identify the news, event or relationship.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 makes a tidy short/long-version reversal, but its content is almost entirely unspecified.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 53\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The rent's paid. Can we keep this evening peaceful? You've only just moved back.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Did you borrow from my mother again?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The landlord has his money. We don't need another family argument.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Mum's coming for dinner. I'll thank her.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Let me thank her privately. I want your first night back to have a second.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D87 makes A restrict disclosure of a consequential truth to prevent a conflict A fears will undo a fragile reunion.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D85 hides A's role in creating past distance while repairing it; here A conceals a current recurring problem because renewed conflict threatens the reunion.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 establishes B's recent return, A3 avoids answering the loan question, and A5 blocks public confirmation to protect a second night together.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Revised b hides likely repeated borrowing and tries to control an imminent dinner conversation; revised a minimizes a relative's request and blocks a phone call.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the unspecified news into an illustrative rent payment, suspected family loan and first night of reunion. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A5 connects concealment to the relationship continuing), logic 5 (A3 evades B2's funding source; A5 redirects B4's planned thanks), relationship 4 (B reasonably seeks and proposes acknowledgment of help), heightening 4 (A5 must manage imminent direct contact), specificity 5 (rent, mother and dinner make the secret playable), brevity/wit 4 (A5's second-night request grows from A1's return). Total 92; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The loan remains an evasively unconfirmed truth, and A5's first/second-night formulation may require understated delivery.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D88-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"7341b0ffc347aec2d102e35bb75d8b6c60827acd82ec4b378fb647b139799ae4\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 explicitly insists on asking first; A5 requests more of B4's attachment before offering A's own.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 sidesteps B2's reciprocal question with acoustics; A5 asks B to elaborate B4's expectation of A's key.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 seeks reciprocity and B4 volunteers vulnerability, changing A's room to negotiate disclosure.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 approaches reciprocal admission but still makes further disclosure from B the condition.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes return to a shared flat; B4's expected key makes the absence concrete.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's acoustics defense grows from A1's quiet-flat question and exposes A's guarded attachment.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Was the flat very quiet while I was away?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Did you miss me?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'm asking about the acoustics here first.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I kept expecting your key.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Good. Tell me that bit before I tell you about mine.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D88 makes A solicit B's attachment while delaying reciprocal vulnerability until B has admitted enough.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D83 tests remembered facts; D88 tests willingness to disclose feeling before A risks the same.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 refuses B2's request for A's feelings, and A5 explicitly orders B's account before A's after B4 reveals longing.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a openly negotiates who admits missing whom first; alternative b approaches attachment indirectly through ownership and preservation of a chair.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after a separate internal reread at 90 with unchanged ratings and evidence. B4's key detail gives A5 a particular disclosure to request, while its vulnerability brings A closer to answering. Hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5's 'mine' has a slightly uncertain referent, and asking for more after B4's admission can make A seem calculating unless vulnerability remains visible.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D88-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d454ee5447ccf7a30de014bd68ac87a7e428fa29700f5149844931a6a3d2f399\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 seeks emotional significance before A5 reveals keeping the cushion, but B4 speaks for unspecified people rather than admitting personal attachment.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 probes B2's ambiguous 'Nobody wanted it'; A5 makes B4's answer the permission for reciprocal disclosure.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 report the chair's status without showing B's own want or investment.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4's answer unlocks A5's previously withheld fact about the cushion.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes an absent person's chair, and A3's wobble supplies a plausible nonemotional explanation.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's wobble-versus-ownership choice efficiently dramatizes the emotional test, and A5 extends the same object.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 81\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You kept my chair by the window. Was that for me?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It was too heavy to move. Why did you take the cushion?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"First, why is there a fresh cup beside it?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I still make two. It's stupid.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"It's not. Ask me about the cushion again.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D88 makes A postpone explaining a private token of attachment until B admits an equivalent attachment first.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Investigating suspicious objects seeks factual explanation; D88 uses those objects to secure emotional disclosure before reciprocating.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 defers B2's cushion question and probes the second cup; only after B4 admits the habit does A5 invite that question again.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Revised b uses reciprocal embarrassment and visible household evidence; retained a uses a direct question about missing A followed by explicit sequencing.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised because original B4 did not securely establish B's own attachment. Preserved the chair and cushion while adding an illustrative second cup. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 withholds and A5 opens up after B4), logic 5 (A3 delays B2's question; A5 returns to it because of B4), relationship 4 (B also deflects before risking embarrassment), heightening 4 (A5 shifts from testing to readiness for disclosure), specificity 5 (chair, cup and cushion anchor the exchange), brevity/wit 4 (A5's repeated invitation conveys a changed emotional condition). Total 92; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 opens the door to disclosure without actually giving it; this preserves continuation but makes the final movement deliberately small.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D89-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"e927ac5b646805f6bd2305e678bafb9146f91ab36a75d0f3ab4b69f53823e685\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 calls the separation healthy; A3 and A5 recast silence and forgotten birthdays as beneficial renewal.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 turns B2's total silence into a thorough reset; A5 turns B4's birthdays into fresh voluntary choices.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 supply increasingly personal evidence against A's optimistic account.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 extends the rationale from past absence to how they can value future birthday observance.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a year apart, but the present reunion setting is unspecified and birthdays remain general.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'No half-measures' follows total silence, while A5's fresh choice directly repurposes B4's lapse.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 88\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That year apart was probably healthy for us.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We didn't speak at all.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"A thorough reset. No half-measures.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We forgot each other's birthdays.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Now remembering them can be a fresh choice.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D89 makes A reinterpret concrete evidence of disconnection as the workings and benefits of a healthy reset.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General optimism merely finds a positive angle; D89 specifically presents the rupture itself as beneficial.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 calls the lack of contact a thorough reset, and A5 claims forgotten birthdays create a healthier basis for remembering them.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a treats prolonged absence as renewal; alternative b treats a failed gathering as information that can improve how the relationship operates.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after an internal reread at 88 with unchanged ratings and evidence. B4 makes the cost more personal, and A5 must explain that exact loss as a future benefit. Hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A1 offers little physical situation, and A5 proposes a potential benefit rather than proving the separation has already helped.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D89-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d4c93f50e1cc5d987d6434cbf2188952d0eca11549307db2f2529180432e1574\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 and A3 frame the failed reunion as useful diagnosis; A5's direction problem does not identify a credible relational benefit.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 recasts B2's disaster and A5 uses B4's separate departures, but the final inference is mostly wordplay.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 repeats A's own disaster label; B4 supplies a fact without a distinct practical want.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds another positive label without developing what the failed connection helped them change.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 names a reunion, but A3's diagnostic material and A5's direction problem remain abstract.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's direction joke connects to B4's departure but weakens the sincerity of the claimed benefit.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 70\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Sunday's disastrous family lunch was good for us. We've finally agreed to meet here, just us sisters.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We only agreed because Dad banned us from his dini